# container_holds_no_view.z -- a collection owns what it holds, and a view owns
# nothing, so a List, a Set and a Map's reference key or value cannot be a
# StringView, whatever the view would view. Static text is `text` (ListVal text,
# MapVV text, SetVal text), owned text a String.
main: function is {
    xs: List StringView
    m: MapRV StringView v: u8
    n: MapVR u8 V: StringView
    s: Set StringView
    print "\{xs.length} \{m.length} \{n.length} \{s.length}"
}
